Verdict: PASS. The fix does what #1019 asked, and the built binary confirms it. I wrote the verdict to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

• **What changed:** the ceiling function now returns a ceiling only where a preset declares a real maximum:
  • GPT-6 presets on openai get 128000.
  • `deepseek keeps its ceiling, because ModelConfig::deepseek` sets 384K for every model id.
  • Everything else gets none, so the warning is skipped instead of comparing against the 4096 request default.
• **Run with the binary:**
  • `--provider ollama --model llama3.3 --max-tokens 16000` no longer prints the false "ceiling 4096" warning.
  • `openai gpt-6-sol --max-tokens 200000` still prints the real 128000 warning, with the same text as before.
• **Callers and tests:** both callers of the changed return type are updated in the diff: the agent build path and the existing preset test. The new tests cover the four rows from the assessment plus custom, zai and minimax. Each row checks first that the old code would have warned, so the test can't pass trivially. The near-miss cases for gpt-6-sol at and below its maximum stay silent.
• **Docs:** docs/src/configuration/models.md doesn't mention the ceiling warning, so the conditional docs step didn't apply.
• **Product surface:** the only user-visible change is one false warning removed. No defaults, flags or startup behavior changed.
